§ `May the old law still be used to deal with my offence`

-- s 34(2)(a)
#ASSERT `May the old law still be used to deal with my offence` `investigating the offence or breach` (Date 28 2 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 34(2): the offence was after the repeal
#ASSERT `May the old law still be used to deal with my offence` `imposing a penalty, or any other remedy or relief, or making or giving an order or a direction, for the offence or breach` (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 34(2)(c): making an order is one of the things the paragraph names
#ASSERT `May the old law still be used to deal with my offence` `making an order for the offence or breach` (Date 28 2 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 34(2)(b): completing a proceeding
#ASSERT `May the old law still be used to deal with my offence` `completing a proceeding for the offence or breach` (Date 28 2 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 34(2): another purpose is not on the closed list (ruling B, fork F11)
#ASSERT `May the old law still be used to deal with my offence` `another purpose` (Date 28 2 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `What does a reference to new legislation that is not yet in force refer to today`

-- s 37: until it comes into force
#ASSERT `What does a reference to new legislation that is not yet in force refer to today` (Date 31 5 2026) TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST `The whole or the corresponding part of the existing legislation`
-- s 37: once in force, the section is silent
#ASSERT `What does a reference to new legislation that is not yet in force refer to today` (Date 1 6 2026) TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 37: not replacing existing legislation
#ASSERT `What does a reference to new legislation that is not yet in force refer to today` (Date 31 5 2026) FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `What does a reference in legislation to repealed legislation mean now`

-- s 38(2)
