§ `On which day does my period end`

-- worked case 1: the Act does not define a year (finding)
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` 3 `years` `from or after the day or the event named` (Date 16 7 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
-- worked case 2
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` 5 `years` `from or after the day or the event named` (Date 15 1 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
-- worked case 3
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` 5 `years` `from or after the day or the event named` (Date 1 9 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
-- worked case 4: s 54 Item 2 and Item 3 (the 30 days start on 2 January)
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` 30 `days` `from or after the day or the event named` (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 31 1 2026)
-- worked case 5: s 56; from 31 December the period starts on 1 January (s 54 Item 2), the ending month is March, its corresponding day is 1 March, so the period ends at the close of 28 February
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` 2 `months` `from or after the day or the event named` (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2026)
-- worked case 6: s 56; starts on 1 February, ending month March, ends immediately before 1 March, which is the close of 29 February (2024 is a leap year)
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` 1 `months` `from or after the day or the event named` (Date 31 1 2024) EQUALS JUST (Date 29 2 2024)
-- worked case 7
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` 1 `years` `from or after the day or the event named` (Date 29 2 2024) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 54 Item 3: adopted on 1 August, notice by the close of 11 August
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` 10 `days` `from or after the day or the event named` (Date 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 11 8 2026)
-- s 56 example 2: starts on 31 October, ends at the close of 30 April
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` 6 `months` `starting or beginning on the day named` (Date 31 10 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 30 4 2027)
-- s 56 example 1
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` 1 `months` `starting or beginning on the day named` (Date 15 2 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 14 3 2026)
-- the Act does not define a week
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` 2 `weeks` `from or after the day or the event named` (Date 2 2 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `On which day does my period end if the legislation names the closing day`

-- s 54 Item 4
