-- s 54 Item 5
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end if the legislation names the closing day` `continuing until the day named` (Date 30 3 2026) EQUALS (Date 30 3 2026)
-- s 54 Item 6
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end if the legislation names the closing day` `ending before the start of the day named` (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS (Date 30 6 2026)

§ `On which day may I first do the second thing if working days must lie between`

-- s 54 Item 7: first event Mon 2 Feb 2026, neither end day counted; the working days between are 3, 4, 5 Feb (Fri 6 Feb is Waitangi Day), 9-13 Feb, 16 Feb, 17 Feb, which is ten, so the earliest second-event day is Wed 18 Feb
#ASSERT `On which day may I first do the second thing if working days must lie between` 10 (Date 2 2 2026) (Date 6 2 2026) (Date 3 4 2026) (Date 6 4 2026) (Date 25 4 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 10 7 2026) (Date 26 10 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 18 2 2026)
-- s 54 Item 7: one working day must lie between Wed 4 Feb and the second event; Thu 5 Feb is that day, so Fri 6 Feb is the earliest (Item 7 asks only that the end days not be counted, not that the second event fall on a working day)
#ASSERT `On which day may I first do the second thing if working days must lie between` 1 (Date 4 2 2026) (Date 6 2 2026) (Date 3 4 2026) (Date 6 4 2026) (Date 25 4 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 10 7 2026) (Date 26 10 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 6 2 2026)

