§ `What is the official version of the legislation taken to prove`

-- s 79(1)(a)
#ASSERT `What is the official version of the legislation taken to prove` `an official version as originally enacted or made` FALSE EQUALS `It is taken to correctly set out the text of the legislation`
-- s 79(3)
#ASSERT `What is the official version of the legislation taken to prove` `an official version that is a consolidation under section 70` TRUE EQUALS `The presumption does not apply: the contrary is shown`
-- s 79(1)(c)(i): paragraph (b) also applies if the legislation is also a consolidation
#ASSERT `What is the official version of the legislation taken to prove` `an official version that is a consolidation and includes changes made under subpart 2` FALSE EQUALS `It is taken to correctly state, as at its stated date, the law enacted or made by the legislation consolidated and by the amendments (paragraph (b)) and by the changes made (paragraph (c)(i)), and is evidence that those changes are authorised by subpart 2`

§ `Must the court take judicial notice of the legislation`

-- s 81
#ASSERT `Must the court take judicial notice of the legislation` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- s 81: not legislation
#ASSERT `Must the court take judicial notice of the legislation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Is the secondary legislation I rely on disallowed because the House did not deal with the motion in time`

-- s 117(1): none of the three events happens by the deadline
#ASSERT `Is the secondary legislation I rely on disallowed because the House did not deal with the motion in time` TRUE (Date 16 4 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- s 117(1): the House disposed of the motion
#ASSERT `Is the secondary legislation I rely on disallowed because the House did not deal with the motion in time` TRUE (Date 16 4 2026) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- s 117(1): no notice of motion
#ASSERT `Is the secondary legislation I rely on disallowed because the House did not deal with the motion in time` FALSE (Date 16 4 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `On what day does the House's amendment of the secondary legislation I rely on take effect`

-- s 119(2)(a): the 28th day after 1 March
#ASSERT `On what day does the House's amendment of the secondary legislation I rely on take effect` (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS (Date 29 3 2026)
-- s 119(2)(b): the later date stated
#ASSERT `On what day does the House's amendment of the secondary legislation I rely on take effect` (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 15 4 2026) EQUALS (Date 15 4 2026)

§ `By what day must the secondary legislation I rely on be confirmed by an Act`

-- s 121: made 1 January, the close of 30 June next year
#ASSERT `By what day must the secondary legislation I rely on be confirmed by an Act` (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS (Date 30 6 2027)
-- s 121: made 1 July, the close of 31 December next year
#ASSERT `By what day must the secondary legislation I rely on be confirmed by an Act` (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS (Date 31 12 2027)

§ `Will the secondary legislation I rely on be revoked on the confirmation deadline`

-- s 123: not confirmed
#ASSERT `Will the secondary legislation I rely on be revoked on the confirmation deadline` TRUE (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- s 124: the confirming provision commences on the deadline, in time
#ASSERT `Will the secondary legislation I rely on be revoked on the confirmation deadline` TRUE (Date 15 3 2026) TRUE (Date 30 6 2027) TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- s 124: commences a day too late
#ASSERT `Will the secondary legislation I rely on be revoked on the confirmation deadline` TRUE (Date 15 3 2026) TRUE (Date 1 7 2027) TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- s 122: the subpart does not apply
#ASSERT `Will the secondary legislation I rely on be revoked on the confirmation deadline` FALSE (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Am I entitled to a refund of a charge imposed under unconfirmed legislation`

-- s 125(1)(a)
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to a refund of a charge imposed under unconfirmed legislation` `a duty, levy or road user charge` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- s 125(1)(a): a levy is one of the three charges named
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to a refund of a charge imposed under unconfirmed legislation` `a levy` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- s 125(2)
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to a refund of a charge imposed under unconfirmed legislation` `an order made under section 5(1) of the Energy Resources Levy Act 1976` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- s 125(3): Part 2 of Schedule 4
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to a refund of a charge imposed under unconfirmed legislation` `a duty, levy or road user charge` TRUE EQUALS FALSE

§ `May I bring a proceeding against the Chief Parliamentary Counsel or an employee of the PCO`

-- s 146: an act in good faith
#ASSERT `May I bring a proceeding against the Chief Parliamentary Counsel or an employee of the PCO` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 146: not in good faith, the section is silent
#ASSERT `May I bring a proceeding against the Chief Parliamentary Counsel or an employee of the PCO` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Does section 26 govern when the secondary legislation I rely on, made before the Act, came into force`

-- Schedule 1 cl 5
#ASSERT `Does section 26 govern when the secondary legislation I rely on, made before the Act, came into force` (Date 31 12 2020) (Date 1 1 2021) EQUALS FALSE
-- Schedule 1 cl 5: made on the main commencement date, not before
#ASSERT `Does section 26 govern when the secondary legislation I rely on, made before the Act, came into force` (Date 1 1 2021) (Date 1 1 2021) EQUALS TRUE
